  "executive_briefing": "The late 2026 tax and trade landscape is defined by the operationalization of the OECD Pillar Two 15% global minimum corporate tax, with over 60 countries actively implementing these rules for multinational enterprises (MNEs) exceeding the \u2007750 million revenue threshold. Governments are modifying effective tax rates and corporate tax incentives to maintain competitiveness, heavily guided by the July 2026 OECD Corporate Tax Statistics report. Digital tax administrations are advancing mandatory e-invoicing, with Singapore's Peppol-based InvoiceNow system leading structured GST reporting. Meanwhile, trade corridors remain highly disrupted due to new presidential tariff actions and upcoming Harmonized Tariff Schedule (HTS) structural adjustments.",
